# mcp-knowledge -- read-only knowledge search/Q&A backend. No ingest tools
# exist here (see app.py) -- this is search/Q&A only. Three tiers, tried in
# order, first configured wins; leave all unset to run the small local
# JSON-file fallback store instead (governance_core/knowledge_store.py).

# ── Tier 1 (preferred): direct Azure AI Search ────────────────────────────
# Queries the SAME index AraTestEnvBE's ragAgent ingests into. This backend
# only ever calls .search() (never upload/delete/merge) -- read-only by code.
# NOTE: as of this writing the configured key is AraTestEnvBE's shared admin
# key (it has to be, since AraTestEnvBE's own ingestion uses the same key to
# write) -- it technically has write capability at the Azure API level even
# though this app never exercises it. Provision a separate Azure AI Search
# QUERY key for this app specifically when someone with management-plane
# access is available, so "read-only" is also a property of the credential.
# AZURE_SEARCH_SERVICE_ENDPOINT=https://<service>.search.windows.net
# AZURE_SEARCH_API_KEY=
# AZURE_SEARCH_INDEX_NAME=ara-prod

# ── Tier 2: HTTP proxy to AraTestEnvBE's ragAgent API ─────────────────────
# Only used if Tier 1 is unset. AraTestEnvBE's ragAgent Document Intelligence
# API (src/ragAgent/api/app.py), default port 8000 per its own README/settings.py.
# KNOWLEDGE_RETRIEVAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Sent as an `x-api-key` header on every Tier-2 request. NOTE: as of this
# writing, AraTestEnvBE's /api/ai-search/* routes do not check this header at
# all (no auth on that side yet) -- setting this doesn't add protection by
# itself, it's forward-compatible with whenever AraTestEnvBE adds a real
# auth check.
# KNOWLEDGE_API_KEY=

KNOWLEDGE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SEC=60

# ── Personal knowledge tier (digest_persoanl_kb.md) ───────────────────────
# NOT AraTest's shared AzureOpenAIService-LanguageModels/
# agenticai-documentintelligence (RG_Agentic_AI) -- this app owns every resource
# it depends on. Values below are placeholders; fill in after the Azure
# resources exist.
#
# Embeddings (text-embedding-3-large): reuses the pre-existing
# `general-usage-resource` (RG_IVA_Prod, eastus2) rather than a new dedicated
# resource -- a deliberate exception made during implementation (digest_persoanl_kb.md
# §0.1's "revised a second time" note), since it already had this exact
# deployment. Use the "Azure OpenAI Legacy API" endpoint from that resource's
# endpoint list, NOT the newer .services.ai.azure.com one -- the openai SDK's
# AzureOpenAI client expects the classic hostname. Automatic TF-IDF fallback if
# this is unset or a call fails.
# GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT=https://general-usage-resource.openai.azure.com/
# GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=
# GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT=text-embedding-3-large
# GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_API_VERSION=2024-12-01-preview
# GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024
#
# Document Intelligence (prebuilt-read) -- ALL personal PDF text extraction, not
# just scanned pages (no local PDF-parsing library in this design -- see
# docintel_client.py's docstring). Unset means PDF upload fails closed with "no
# text could be extracted", same as any other extraction miss. Still a NEW
# dedicated resource per the original plan (e.g. governance-agent-docintel in
# RG_IVA_Prod), Standard S0 tier -- F0 caps at 500 pages/month and only reads
# the first 2 pages of any document, unusable for real uploads.
# GOVERNANCE_DOCINTEL_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/
# GOVERNANCE_DOCINTEL_API_KEY=
# GOVERNANCE_DOCINTEL_TIMEOUT_SEC=60
#
# Personal-KB storage: reuses the SAME GOVERNANCE_COSMOS_* vars gateway/.env.local
# already defines for the policy store (new containers, same account) -- falls
# back to a local JSON file (.governance-state/personal_knowledge.json) if unset.
#
# Company-KB hybrid search: the direct Azure AI Search tier (tier 1) now ALSO
# embeds the query (via the SAME GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_* resource above, no
# dedicated resource) and passes it alongside the keyword search for
# server-side hybrid/RRF fusion against the index's existing `embedding`
# field (3072-dim, already populated -- no reindexing/blob change needed).
# Unset GOVERNANCE_EMBEDDING_* -> falls back to keyword-only, same as before
# this existed. This timeout is intentionally short: it's on the critical
# path of a live chat turn, unlike personal-KB ingest.
# GOVERNANCE_KB_VECTOR_EMBED_TIMEOUT_SEC=3.0
#
# Per-upload size cap (bytes) and per-owner document-count cap -- rejected with
# a clean error before extraction/embedding runs (digest_persoanl_kb.md §4's
# open item, now resolved). Tune the size cap down if the actual Document
# Intelligence resource's confirmed inline-body limit is tighter than 20MB.
# GOVERNANCE_PERSONAL_KB_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=20971520
# GOVERNANCE_PERSONAL_KB_MAX_DOCS_PER_OWNER=300

# ── Reranker (bge-reranker-v2-m3) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Second stage of the embed/search-then-rerank funnel, applied to all three
# tiers above (personal, and company direct/proxy/local) -- see
# ../howtousereranker.md and ../governance_core/rerank_client.py. This process
# is what actually calls it, not the gateway. Get the key from whoever
# deployed the reranker service (root-only on the VM, never committed). Unset
# means every search()/answer() falls back to its pre-rerank order
# (cosine/TF-IDF/upstream-tier ranking) -- fails soft, never breaks KB search.
# RERANKER_API_KEY=
# RERANKER_BASE_URL=http://20.120.220.8:8091
# RERANKER_TIMEOUT_SEC=15
#
# Candidate-pool width fetched before reranking (shared by all tiers/files
# that call rerank_client.py -- knowledge_store.py, personal_knowledge_store.py,
# and this file's own _direct_search/_remote_search).
# GOVERNANCE_KB_RERANK_CANDIDATE_POOL=30
#
# Skip the reranker call entirely when the candidate pool is already within
# this many items of the requested limit (default 0 -- skip only when there's
# truly nothing left to narrow, e.g. a 3-chunk personal KB asked for limit=5).
# Raise it to also skip reranking small edges (e.g. 6 candidates for limit=5).
# Shared by the same three call sites as the pool width above.
# GOVERNANCE_KB_RERANK_SKIP_MARGIN=0
#
# Personal KB only: below this many total chunks for an owner, skip the
# cosine-narrowing stage and rerank the whole corpus directly (see
# personal_knowledge_store.py's module docstring for why).
# GOVERNANCE_PERSONAL_KB_VECTORIZE_THRESHOLD=40

# Local listener port (the gateway reaches this on 127.0.0.1)
KNOWLEDGE_PORT=8050

# Hosts allowed by the MCP transport (comma-separated). localhost is always
# allowed; the gateway calls this backend on 127.0.0.1, so nothing extra needed.
KNOWLEDGE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
